<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on 91-day</p>
<p>Lithuanian Treasury bills at Monday's auction and all of the 50</p>
<p>million litas issue was sold as the issue was oversubscribed,</p>
<p>the Bank of Lithuania said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 10.58 percent, down from the 11.05</p>
<p>percent offered to bidders at the last auction for 91-day paper</p>
<p>on April 7.</p>
<p>The settlement date is April 17 and the bills mature on</p>
<p>July 17.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas except for days and</p>
<p>yields.</p>
<p>SOLD  DAYS  MIN/MAX YIELD  AV. YIELD   LAST AV. YIELD  DEMAND</p>
<p>50    91    10.07/10.95     10.58	 11.05	   114.727</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
